# OpenSpec language — English only

All OpenSpec work under `openspec/` is **English**, permanently.

## Required

1. `openspec/config.yaml`, proposals, designs, tasks, specs, and archives: English only.
2. Structural headings and `SHALL` / `MUST` stay English (already the OpenSpec convention).
3. Do not write new German OpenSpec prose; if you touch a German leftover, translate it to English in the same pass.
4. Product UI may still offer German (see `ui-locale`); that is app chrome, not OpenSpec authoring language.

## Do not

- New OpenSpec changes in German
- Mixing German requirements with English scenarios in the same spec
- Treating chat/UI language (DE/EN) as the OpenSpec authoring language
